---
import ComponentDoc from '../../layouts/ComponentDoc.astro';
import Section from '@esa/docs/Section.astro';
import Preview from '@esa/docs/Preview.astro';
import Api from '@esa/docs/Api.astro';
import PropsTable from '@esa/docs/PropsTable.astro';
import PageHeader from '@esa/ecology/esa-page-header.astro';
import Button from '@esa/ecology/esa-button.astro';

const props = [
  { name: 'title', type: 'string', description: 'The page’s name, as it appears in navigation and breadcrumbs (required). Rendered as the <h1>.' },
  { name: 'meta', type: 'EsaMetaPair[]', description: 'Identifying facts about the record this page shows, as {label, value} pairs. Renders as a definition list under the title: a wrapping row at width, one stack per pair below it. Both parts are required. A period pair states its calendar: "Calendar Q2 2026", not "Q2".' },
  { name: 'eyebrow', type: 'string', description: 'The named thing this page sits inside: a section, a report, a person, a record id. A proper noun or a short label, never a sentence.' },
  { name: 'icon', type: 'string', description: 'esa-icon registry name for the eyebrow’s leading glyph, e.g. "award" (eyebrow only).' },
  { name: 'prominence', type: "'page-title' | 'display'", default: "'page-title'", description: 'Title scale: the page-title role (default) or the oversized display role for a hero.' },
  { name: 'as', type: "'header' | 'div' | 'section'", default: "'header'", description: 'The host element tag.' },
];

const slots = [
  { name: 'breadcrumbs', type: 'slot', description: 'Above the title — host an esa-breadcrumbs here. Mutually exclusive in spirit with eyebrow.' },
  { name: 'actions', type: 'slot', description: 'Right-aligned, top-aligned with the title block — buttons or links.' },
];
---
<ComponentDoc name="Page Header" category="Layout & Sections" slug="esa-page-header" type=".astro" status="stable"
  summary="The standard prototype page top: optional breadcrumbs OR an eyebrow (with a leading icon), a title (page-title role, or the oversized display role for a hero), and a right-aligned actions slot.">

  <Section id="preview" title="Preview">
    <p>The default form: a page-title-scale heading with an actions slot. The container is neutral and transparent; color is the consumer’s job.</p>
    <Preview align="start" code={`<PageHeader title="Requirements">
  <Button slot="actions" color="primary" icon="plus">New requirement</Button>
</PageHeader>`}>
      <div style="width: 100%;">
        <PageHeader title="Requirements">
          <Button slot="actions" color="primary" icon="plus">New requirement</Button>
        </PageHeader>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="no-description" title="There is no description slot">
    <p>This component takes no <code>lede</code>, <code>subtitle</code>, or <code>description</code>. A page header carries the page’s name and its actions; a sentence explaining the page to its reader is text <em>about</em> the page rather than <em>of</em> it, and the page’s own data and structure are what say what it is.</p>
    <p>Identifying facts go in <code>meta</code>, which takes labeled pairs rather than free text — see below. A figure the page exists to report is a stat: put it in an <code>esa-stat</code> under the header, where it reads at stat scale.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="meta" title="Meta pairs">
    <p>Each entry in <code>meta</code> is a <code>{`{ label, value }`}</code> pair: the label is the field's name in the record, the value is what is stored there. Both parts are required.</p>
    <p>That is why it is a prop and not a slot. A slot takes anything, and what it took was a row of facts glued together with separators — <q>SFO, Shoreline Protection Program, Beacon compliance platform</q> — where a client, a program and a platform are three different kinds of thing and nothing on the line says which is which. A pair cannot be written that way.</p>
    <p>A period pair states the calendar it counts by. This domain runs fiscal years and water years alongside calendar ones, and a compliance figure means a different span under each.</p>
    <Preview align="start" code={`<PageHeader
  title="Quarterly Compliance Summary"
  meta={[
    { label: 'Project', value: 'Delta Conveyance Project' },
    { label: 'Reporting period', value: 'Calendar Q2 2026' },
    { label: 'Lead agency', value: 'DWR' },
  ]}>
  <Button slot="actions" color="ghost" appearance="outline" icon="download">Export</Button>
</PageHeader>`}>
      <div style="width: 100%;">
        <PageHeader
          title="Quarterly Compliance Summary"
          meta={[
            { label: 'Project', value: 'Delta Conveyance Project' },
            { label: 'Reporting period', value: 'Calendar Q2 2026' },
            { label: 'Lead agency', value: 'DWR' },
          ]}>
          <Button slot="actions" color="ghost" appearance="outline" icon="download">Export</Button>
        </PageHeader>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="hero" title="Eyebrow + display prominence (hero)">
    <p>For a landing or hero, add an <code>eyebrow</code> (with an optional leading <code>icon</code>) and bump the title to the display role with <code>prominence="display"</code>. The actions here are link-buttons — <code>esa-button</code> with an <code>href</code>.</p>
    <Preview align="start" code={`<PageHeader
  eyebrow="Annual Report"
  icon="award"
  prominence="display"
  title="2026 in Review">
  <Button slot="actions" color="primary" href="/report">Read the report</Button>
  <Button slot="actions" color="ghost" appearance="outline" href="/data">View the data</Button>
</PageHeader>`}>
      <div style="width: 100%;">
        <PageHeader eyebrow="Annual Report" icon="award" prominence="display" title="2026 in Review">
          <Button slot="actions" color="primary" href="#">Read the report</Button>
          <Button slot="actions" color="ghost" appearance="outline" href="#">View the data</Button>
        </PageHeader>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="breadcrumbs" title="With breadcrumbs">
    <p>Host an <code>esa-breadcrumbs</code> in the <code>breadcrumbs</code> slot for a record or nested page.</p>
    <Preview align="start" code={`<PageHeader title="Permit #4471" eyebrow="Filed 12 days ago">
  <nav slot="breadcrumbs">Permits / Active / #4471</nav>
  <Button slot="actions" color="ghost" appearance="outline" icon="pencil">Edit</Button>
</PageHeader>`}>
      <div style="width: 100%;">
        <PageHeader title="Permit #4471" eyebrow="Filed 12 days ago">
          <nav slot="breadcrumbs" style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary, #555);">Permits / Active / #4471</nav>
          <Button slot="actions" color="ghost" appearance="outline" icon="pencil">Edit</Button>
        </PageHeader>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="api" title="API">
    <Api props={props} />
    <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Slots</h3>
    <PropsTable rows={slots} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="accessibility" title="Accessibility">
    <ul class="a11y">
      <li>The title is the page <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> — there should be exactly one per page; keep heading order sensible below it.</li>
      <li>The host defaults to a <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> landmark; use <code>as="div"</code> when the header is nested inside another landmark.</li>
      <li>The eyebrow icon is decorative (rendered via <code>esa-icon</code>, <code>aria-hidden</code>) — the eyebrow text carries the meaning.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

</ComponentDoc>
